2026-10-03 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.5.2 (menus and exit confirmation)

	* File, VM, and Help commands are grouped, and each command is listed once.
	  Exit is the last item on File. Apple commands live under VM → Apple.
	  Disk, import, host, recovery, storage, tools, lab, and diagnostics each
	  have their own submenu.
	* Closing AQEMU asks “Are you sure you want to exit?” Running virtual
	  machines are stopped only after you confirm. Don’t ask me again and
	  Preferences → Ask before exiting remember the choice.
	* Disabled menu items draw in grey on Windows and Linux. Configure WSL,
	  the WSL dashboard, and WHPX health stay visible and are disabled when
	  the host is not Windows.

2026-10-02 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.5.1 (boot logo, guest detection, host audio)

	* SeaBIOS on 32-bit and 64-bit PCs shows resources/bootsplash.bmp for 3 seconds.
	  Settings and each machine can turn the logo off. UEFI firmware does not draw it.
	* OVF import maps old Windows names (95, 98, ME, NT, 2000, XP) to the matching
	  profile and i386 PC, not Generic Linux on x86_64. Both wizards use the full
	  OS catalog embedded in the app.
	* The Windows package picks a host audiodev the bundled QEMU actually has.
	  Playback prefers spice. DirectSound and SDL are not offered on Windows ARM.
	* Store builds start qemu-system-i386 from the package. A developer qemu.exe
	  under an MSYS tree is not used.
	* The bundled QEMU tree stays unmodified upstream 11.0.2. The audiodev device
	  patch is no longer applied before configure.
	* The menu bar no longer draws a box around File, VM, and Help. Dark mode
	  follows the OS theme on Linux, Windows, and macOS instead of leaving
	  white bars.

2026-10-01 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.5.0 (QEMU catalog and custom wraps)

	* User guide: docs/LAB_1.5.0.md. Documentation index: docs/README.md.
	  GDB, qemu-nbd, and the isolated socket NIC listen on localhost.
	  virtiofs honors read-only. Windows 11 ARM always gets a private VARS
	  file, and swtpm is started with the VM when it is installed.

	* Stage A, small stock-QEMU niches:
	  - VM → Lab replaces the raw hostfwd text box with a port table, SSH/RDP/HTTP
	    presets, and a user-net air-gap next to the existing SMB fields.
	  - Help → Support bundle writes a redacted settings and command log.
	  - GDB stub, guest memory dump, disk throttle, cache and aio presets,
	    floppy/SD/MTD/pflash, RTC, direct boot, aarch64=off, fw_cfg, and
	    sandbox presets (Linux only on Windows).
	  - Help → QEMU catalog and bundle auditor, first-run cards, argument
	    snippets, period video and audio presets, PowerNV and s390x wizard
	    profiles, and an optional TCG plugin picker.
	  - File → Convert disk reuses the existing 4Kn control.

	* Stage B, medium studios:
	  - Accelerator policy shows the effective choice. WHPX is not offered for
	    a guest this host cannot accelerate. A failed WHPX probe offers Force TCG.
	  - TPM and Secure Boot stay on the existing swtpm socket and OVMF VARS.
	  - VM → Manage Snapshots is now the snapshot timeline.
	  - Command diff, QMP scratchpad, chardev lines, SPICE agent notes,
	    tablet and keyboard toggles, smartcard when usb-ccid is listed,
	    migration, dirty bitmaps, qemu-nbd, TAP and bridge, multi-NIC
	    templates, USB redirect rules, CPU pin, guest agent, lab packs,
	    linked clones, tagged groups, device_add, LUKS secrets outside the
	    VM file, block jobs, the WSL dashboard, and WoA presets.

	* Stage C, large stock features:
	  - Shared folders keep one -virtfs path and add mount tag, security model,
	    and read-only. virtiofsd is used only when the host has it.
	  - Chain Studio, retro Force TCG packs, the multi-arch gallery,
	    record/replay, multi-head, VirGL on Linux, VFIO on Linux, and a
	    firmware library that clones a private VARS file.

	* Stage D, bring-your-own wraps:
	  - Quickemu .conf import, an xemu picker (README only, no Microsoft ROMs),
	    Android SDK detection, OpenCore beside the existing macOS profiles,
	    Nitro and SEV/TDX on Linux, virtio-ramfb only when that QEMU lists it,
	    and a Darwin research shell that is not Inferno and does not boot
	    SpringBoard.
	  - Unicorn, Qiling, WinAFL, Firecracker, crosvm, Xenia, Dolphin, RPCS3,
	    Anbox, Waydroid, Limbo, Xen, dead XNU trees, and Corellium stay skipped.
	    vmapple stays a Mac-host note.

	* Network page port table, support zip, and Windows 11 TPM step:
	  - The NIC hostfwd box is a port table with SSH, RDP, and HTTP presets.
	    It still saves hostfwd= rules.
	  - Help → Support bundle writes a zip of redacted settings, the QEMU
	    command, the boot log, and the version.
	  - The Windows 11 ARM wizard step can enable the existing swtpm socket
	    and a private OVMF VARS file.
	  - fw_cfg in VM → Lab is a name, kind, and file-or-string table.
	  - Saved hostfwd rules reload as proto, host port, guest IP, and guest port.
	    The support zip redacts OSK, IPSW, and secret arguments. Failed starts
	    stop virtiofsd and vsock helpers. Snapshot overlays become the disk.
	    WHPX health is Windows-only. Import OVA opens appliance import.
	    Record/replay Off clears -icount. VirGL uses virtio-gpu-gl-pci.
	    Auto clears a Lab-owned TCG or WSL launch. Disk throttle is on -drive.
	    Windows LUKS secret files are readable only by the current user.

	* 1.4.2 remains the Store build already submitted. Store copy still does
	  not say AQEMU includes Xbox, Android, or macOS. Issue #42 stays open.

2026-10-01 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.4.2 (Storage Recovery, TrueNAS Lab & Host Audio)

	* Storage recovery:
	  - File → Storage Recovery… and a Recover storage card in the New VM wizard.
	  - Recovery checkpoints copy disks onto overlays, then rewire the VM only after
	    the manifest is written. Discard deletes only files named in that manifest.
	    Keep leaves the overlays in place and does not modify the original disks.
	  - Probe text stays at detected labels and a probable pool. The guest decides
	    whether an import or repair worked.

	* TrueNAS and folder-backed disks:
	  - Appliance import recognizes TrueNAS and FreeNAS, forces 4Kn when the
	    descriptor or a ZFS label says so, and keeps disk serials on VirtIO-SCSI.
	  - Guest OS → TrueNAS / Storage: a lab VM, folder-backed empty disks, and a
	    four-VM storage network on one multicast bus. No pool and no image are shipped.
	  - The VM Storage tab can read TrueNAS pools and snapshots when integration
	    is enabled. The API token stays in settings, not in the VM file.

	* Audio:
	  - File → Audio… sets the computer-wide backend, devices, and buffer options.
	  - VM → Audio… can override that profile. Intel HDA can be playback only,
	    playback and microphone, or microphone only.
	  - Bundled QEMU accepts DirectSound and SDL input and output device names.

	* Microsoft Store builds keep their own settings and start only the QEMU
	  shipped beside AQEMU. 1.4.1 remains the previous Store release.

