2026-09-27 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.3.2 (4Kn Native Sector Disks & Multi-Platform QEMU Build System)

	* Native 4096-Byte (4Kn) Sector Disk & 512e Emulation:
	  - New VM Wizard: Added Sector Size selector (Default 512n, 4096B Native 4Kn, 512e)
	    to both Typical storage page and Custom Devices page.
	  - TrueNAS / ZFS Backup Compatibility: Directly import existing VM disks and assign
	    native 4096B sector size geometry without format conversions.
	  - Automatic Bus Elevation: Elevated legacy IDE disk buses to VirtIO when 4Kn is
	    selected, and safely clamped IDE/AHCI to 512e mode to prevent QEMU startup errors.
	  - Properties Window: Added dedicated Sector Size dropdown directly on the Hard Disk
	    tab with bidirectional synchronization with Advanced Device settings.
	  - Create HDD Image: Added QCOW2 cluster size & 4K alignment options (4 KB through 2 MB)
	    to eliminate write amplification on 4Kn and ZFS record-size workloads.
	  - Core Engine: Fixed QEMU CLI generation to emit block sizes exclusively to frontend
	    -device options (virtio-blk-pci, nvme, scsi-hd) rather than backend -drive options.

	* Multi-Platform QEMU Build Scripts & Special Targets:
	  - Added unified build scripts for special QEMU targets (applesoc / ChefKiss Inferno
	    and reims / steelbrain Reims vGPU) across Windows on ARM, Linux, and Windows x64.
	  - Automated dependency resolution for lzfse, nettle, hogweed, gmp, and Meson/Ninja.
	  - Automated recursive runtime DLL bundling for Windows x64 and ARM64 Snapdragon devices.
	  - System tray icon scaling: Fixed Wayland / wf-panel-pi panel height bulging on Linux.

2026-09-25 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.3.1 (Embedded Canvas Scaling & Dynamic USB Overhaul)

	* Embedded Display Canvas Auto-Stretch & Scaling:
	  - Fixed QEMU hardware scanout forcing bug: In embedded session mode, never
	    append `,xres=...,yres=...` to virtio-gpu-pci / virtio-vga. Forcing scanout
	    dimensions was locking the virtual GPU to a fixed buffer, causing guest
	    VGA desktops (e.g. 1024x768) to be letterboxed with solid black borders
	    and breaking in-guest resolution switching.
	  - Map `virtio` on x86 PC/Q35 to `virtio-vga` instead of `virtio-gpu-pci` to
	    ensure full legacy VGA register and mode switching compatibility during
	    early boot and desktop transitions.
	  - VncView & Spice_View: Removed aspect-ratio letterboxing clamping; views now
	    unconditionally stretch the guest frame across the full widget canvas
	    (`painter.drawImage( rect(), frame, frame.rect() )`).
	  - Implemented `sizeHint()` and `minimumSizeHint()` returning `QSize(1, 1)`
	    along with `QSizePolicy::Expanding` across display widgets and containers
	    to allow dynamic resizing without minimum-size locking.
	  - MachineView (QScrollArea): Disabled scrollbars (`Qt::ScrollBarAlwaysOff`),
	    set `Qt::AlignLeft | Qt::AlignTop` with zeroed margins, and explicitly
	    resize and position `View` at `(0, 0, width, height)` on all resize events.
	  - Synchronized VM_Session_Widget: Viewport geometry is immediately propagated
	    to embedded views during window resize, maximize, and fullscreen switches.
	  - Input coordinate transformation: Dynamic pointer matrix maps host widget
	    coordinates directly to guest framebuffer width/height with boundary clamping.

	* USB Passthrough & Hotplug Overhaul:
	  - Automatic modern USB 3.0 XHCI hub (`aqemu_usb_hub.0`) injection for x86 (Q35)
	    and ARM (virt) architectures, replacing legacy EHCI/UHCI speed matching bugs.
	  - Asynchronous, tracked QMP USB hotplugging (`device_add` and `device_del`)
	    with error handling, non-blocking UI, and dynamic status labels in toolbar.
	  - Added safety warning when attempting to pass through primary host input devices
	    (keyboards/mice) to prevent host lockouts.
	  - Host USB device enumeration: Full `/sys/bus/usb/devices` fallback handling
	    for composite devices, multi-interface hardware, and host-based printers
	    (such as Ricoh SP 211 / DDST GDI printers).

	* Multiplatform & Build System:
	  - Added CMake toolchain profile for Windows on ARM (`resources/cmake/toolchains/generic-win-arm64.cmake`).
	  - Updated Meson build configuration for Raspberry Pi 5 ARM64 optimizations.
	  - Added Out-of-Memory (OOM-killer, exit code 137/-9) diagnostics and ram-tuning
	    guidance in `Virtual_Machine::QEMU_Finished`.
	  - Added `*.bz2` to `.gitignore` to prevent generated documentation archives from polluting tree.
	  - Windows subsystem: Set `WIN32_EXECUTABLE TRUE` in CMakeLists.txt and `win_subsystem: 'windows'`
	    in meson.build to eliminate the extraneous terminal/console window on launch (Fixes #53).

	* Command Line & Script Export:
	  - Use `^` Windows caret line continuations instead of Unix `\` backslashes when displaying
	    or exporting QEMU commands on Windows (Fixes #55).
	  - Added support for exporting Windows Batch scripts (`.bat` / `.cmd`) and PowerShell scripts
	    (`.ps1`) with native path separators, quoting, argument forwarding, and line continuations (Fixes #55).

	* QEMU Installation Discovery & Disambiguation:
	  - Disambiguated built-in (portable, alongside aqemu.exe) from system-installed QEMU (e.g.
	    `C:\Program Files\qemu` or `/usr/bin`) across First Start Wizard and Settings dialogs.
	  - Added `AQ_Get_System_QEMU_Dir()` and `AQ_Has_System_QEMU()` helpers alongside `AQ_Get_Bundled_QEMU_Dir()`
	    to prevent mislabeling system-wide installs as portable bundled builds (Fixes #52).

	* Storage Device Block Sizes (4096 / 4Kn Sectors):
	  - Added configurable `logical_block_size` and `physical_block_size` (512 vs 4096 bytes)
	    to `VM_Native_Storage_Device`, Add New Device UI, and VM XML configurations (Fixes #50).
	  - Emits `,logical_block_size=...,physical_block_size=...` for `virtio-blk-pci`, `scsi-hd`,
	    `ide-hd`, `nvme`, and direct `-drive` flags for modern Advanced Format 4Kn disks (Fixes #50).

	* Packaging & Store Sandboxing:
	  - Enhanced `installer/build-msix.ps1` with automated `windeployqt` integration, GCC/MinGW
	    runtime DLL bundling, and recursive PE import dependency resolution to prevent DLL load
	    errors on Microsoft Store and MSIX packaged installations (Fixes #54).

	* Documentation & Project Links:
	  - Updated `README.md` to point directly to active GitHub project repository and release
	    pages, removing dead `neonsovereign.store` domain references (Fixes #48).

2026-08-08 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.3.0 (Apple SoC Inferno + Reims WSL)

	* Version bump to 1.3.0 across code, MSI/MSIX, WiX, and packaging docs.
	* Apple SoC / iOS (ChefKiss Inferno):
	  - Inferno launch profile: trustcache, ticket, SEP FW/ROM, usb-conn, kaslr-off,
	    multi-ns NVMe + apple-nvram + SEP pflash image set under the VM folder.
	  - MACHINE tab owns all Inferno file paths (kernel, DeviceTree, trustcache,
	    ticket, SEP FW/ROM, optional SecureROM, IPSW) and USB remote / kaslr-off.
	    Launch never invents missing paths or injects default -append; Start validates
	    required MACHINE-tab fields and fails with a clear message instead.
	  - On Windows, applesoc is forced through WSL Linux qemu-system-applesoc
	    (UNIX sockets / companion restore; not Windows PE alone).
	  - File → Apple SoC Restore: companion helper; one-click SSH upload of IPSW
	    + idevicerestore inside the companion (sshpass via WSL).
	  - File → Apply iOS filesystem patches… (also MACHINE tab + Restore dialog +
	    post-restore prompt): InfernoFSPatcher + LaunchDaemons on the guest root
	    NVMe via WSL KVM helper — not the companion. Required for SpringBoard;
	    clears Restore ramdisk (-initrd) on success. Bundles extras/Inferno scripts.
	  - Session toolbar (Apple SoC): Home / Side / Vol / SOS / More… / Pad / Net via
	    Inferno F-key sendkey; floating pad is neutral (not an iPhone bezel).
	  - File / VM → Guest Internet / iOS Device Tools… (toolbar Net): Enable guest
	    internet (reverse-tether) on the companion — usbmuxd MODE=3 + NetworkManager
	    Shared on USB/NCM (not the AQEMU Network NIC tab). Marks Ubuntu ethernet
	    managed so Shared activation is not “strictly unmanaged”. Diagnose USB /
	    idevice; IPA install via ideviceinstaller (auto-apt if missing); screenshot.
	  - extras/Inferno/iOS_Installation.md: starter + re-install walkthrough
	    (restore, FS patches, internet, IPA vs .deb, 8 GiB vs 32 GiB root).
	    File → iOS Firmware Tool forges restore/SEP tickets and packs SEP firmware
	    in-app (bundled create_*ticket.py; img4 / pyimg4). File → Configure sets
	    Python / pyimg4 / img4 paths (PATH fallback if empty).
	    wipe-ios-nvme.ps1 for partial-flash / clean NAND. Default auto-created root
	    is 8 GiB; grow sparse to 32 GiB before restore for App Store / large IPAs.
	    FS-patch helper selects the iOS NVMe by skipping the cloud-image boot disk
	    (works for 8 GiB and 32 GiB roots). Companion SSH uses accept-new + a
	    dedicated known_hosts file (loopback only).
	  - Restore ramdisk (-initrd) also sets boot-mode=enter_recovery so NVRAM
	    auto-boot=true cannot skip recovery on re-restore.
	  - Apple SoC QEMU stop: short summary first (full kernel-patch dump stays in
	    qemu-boot.log / Error Log); Copy on error dialogs is usable.
	  - Embedded VNC: sticky mouse grab no longer steals File/toolbar; leave and
	    chrome clicks release grab.
	  - Wizard + main UI fields for Inferno firmware paths and USB remote type.
	* Hardware-accelerated Intel macOS (Reims):
	  - Always uses Linux qemu-system-reims3d under WSL with reims-vgpu-pci.
	  - Documents AMD and NVIDIA host GPUs via WSLg Vulkan (not Windows PE Reims).
	  - Reims computer type locks Video Card to reims-vgpu-pci only (UI/wizard/args);
	    cirrus/std from the PE probe catalog are never offered or persisted.
	  - Product display: -display none + embedded VNC for OpenCore/early boot.
	    QEMU SDL/GTK (Separate QEMU window) is blocked for Reims on WSL (DRI3).
	    REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW defaults off: Mesa Dozen on WSLg NVIDIA can segfault in
	    vkCreateDevice and kill QEMU; opt-in under Advanced Settings → WSL.
	  - Wizard/start injects reims-vgpu-efi.efi into OpenCore and prefers OVMF_CODE_4M.
	* WSL: prompt for distro/username on boot when missing; optional password can be
	  saved securely in Windows Credential Manager (never AQEMU.ini). KVM access
	  prefers wsl -u root, with sudo -S stdin fallback when Remember is enabled.
	  Reims VM provision/start auto-installs native-arch Mesa Dozen (dzn)
	  Vulkan-on-D3D12 ICD in WSL (ignores foreign multiarch dzn; strips
	  conflicting mesa-vulkan-drivers:<foreign-arch>). Treats native
	  libvulkan_dzn as ready even when vulkaninfo segfaults/lists nothing.
	  Probe Dozen via wsl -e (not wsl --) so login-shell $(…) expansion cannot
	  falsely report the ICD missing. Reims attach uses pci-bridge +
	  reims-vgpu-gop.rom (UEFI GOP); Intel/Reims prefer OSX-KVM OVMF_CODE_4M
	  over stock edk2 when available. Machine -machine path props rewritten for WSL.

