2026-07-23 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 1.0.0

	* Version bump to 1.0.0 — first public “curtain” release for community testing.
	* QEMU CLI parity waves: Advanced Options for NUMA, watchdog, TPM, secrets,
	  incoming migrate, SMBIOS, fw_cfg, audiodev, icount/sandbox, richer chardev.
	* Blockdev graph editor + migrate progress/cancel (QMP) UI.
	* VM-start UX: busy dialog, async QMP connect (no UI freeze).
	* Guest profile polish: Solaris 11.4 x86 recipe, AIX/pseries (no WHPX/floppy/IDE),
	  OS/2 / ReactOS / Win9x / XP proven defaults in the wizard.
	* Windows: pure TCG for non-x86 guests (ppc64 etc.); quoted Additional Args;
	  qemu-img VMDK size parse fix; quieter startup / clearer breadcrumbs.
	* README refreshed for testers; Windows portable zip = AQEMU + QEMU 11.0.2.

2026-07-23 Chronic Engineering — AQEMU 0.9.9 Windows release

	* Version bump to 0.9.9.
	* README: GitHub Releases are free portable builds without auto-updates;
	  Microsoft Store will be the update channel once published.
	* Windows portable zip bundles AQEMU + QEMU 11.0.2 + UEFI firmware.

2026-07-23 Chronic Engineering — Intel macOS match host / 4K resolution via OpenCore

	* Enable General → Resolution for Intel macOS (not only VirtIO-GPU).
	* Default new Intel macOS VMs to Native (host physical pixels, DPI-aware).
	* On start, patch OpenCore FAT config.plist Resolution (+ ForceResolution) via mtools.
	* Add 3840x2160 / 4096x2160 presets; raise vmware-svga VRAM to 256MB for ≥1440p.
	* Docs updated in docs/intel-macos-gpu.md.

2026-07-23 Chronic Engineering — Intel macOS AMD GPU passthrough UI + software defaults

	Conditional AMD Metal / VFIO UI (community)
	* Detect host GPUs (Linux sysfs; Windows Win32_VideoController).
	* Hide AMD passthrough controls when no AMD display GPU is present.
	* Grey out when AMD is present but host cannot VFIO (Windows/WSL); enable on
	  bare-metal Linux. Passthrough stays off by default (install with software VGA).
	* Persist GPU_Passthrough / PCI BDFs / optional ROM; emit vfio-pci (+ HDMI audio).
	* Refuse start when passthrough is on under Windows/WSL — WSLg ≠ PCIe assignment.
	* Docs: docs/intel-macos-gpu.md

	Software path (global default)
	* Intel macOS continues to use vmware-svga,vgamem_mb=128 when not passthrough.

2026-07-23 Chronic Engineering — Intel macOS on Windows (WSL/KVM) + installer pipeline

	Intel macOS guest support (OpenCore + AppleSMC OSK)
	* New Intel macOS wizard page and main-window settings: OpenCore path,
	  Recovery/BaseSystem installer path, OSK, prefer-WSL checkbox.
	* Preserve / repair macOS list icon (default_macos.png); profile flag in .aqemu.
	* QEMU args: q35, ich9-ahci, OVMF, isa-applesmc + OSK validation (reject
	  Proxmox/network junk pasted as OSK), smbios type=2.
	* CPU: Skylake-Client-v4 + GenuineIntel (+invtsc/kvm/vmware-cpuid-freq under
	  WSL KVM). Penryn alone often died with "still waiting for root device".
	* NIC: force virtio-net-pci for Intel macOS (e1000-82545em often has no link
	  in Sonoma/Monterey Recovery → "internet connection required").
	* System disk always on AHCI for OpenCore visibility (not VirtIO without kexts).

	OpenCore / installer media correctness
	* Detect Apple Partition Map (MIST/Pyenb "*.iso") vs true ISO9660.
	* LongQT OpenCore ISO enables OpenPartitionDxe.efi but ships without the file;
	  AQEMU extracts BOOT.img, injects bundled OpenPartitionDxe.efi, and boots that
	  FAT image so APM installers are visible and UUID-stable for the kernel.
	* Fallback: raw HFS partition offset= when PartitionDxe prep is unavailable.
	* scripts/patch-longqt-boot.sh helper; third_party/opencore/OpenPartitionDxe.efi
	  copied next to aqemu.exe at build time.
	* Note: incomplete third-party MIST full ISOs can fail mid-install (missing
	  x86_64BaseSystem.dmg). Prefer OSX-KVM BaseSystem.img + network install, or a
	  LongQT full installer ISO attached as CD-ROM.

	Windows ↔ WSL/KVM launch
	* New WSL_Launch.cpp/.h: path rewrite (file.filename=), wsl -e (not bash -c)
	  so OSK "(c)" and spaced paths survive, orphan QEMU kill on stop/restart.
	* WSL_Ensure_KVM_Access: chmod /dev/kvm, kvm group, udev rule; set
	  kvm.ignore_msrs=1 (required for macOS) and persist via modprobe.d.
	* Audio backend selection that works under WSL (avoid host-only dsound/pa).
	* Quoted/normalized disk and firmware paths (AQ_Normalize_File_Path,
	  AQ_Qemu_Drive_File_Key) for spaces under Program Files / OSX ISO folders.

	Wizard / OS catalog and other guest UX
	* Expanded wizard_trees.json / os profiles; QEMU-aligned System_Info captions.
	* Prefer host-native accel when guest arch matches; TCG otherwise.
	* Error log Copy button; Spice/session widget polish; Advanced Options macOS UI.
	* Mac OS Classic PPC template; gitignore for local OSX-KVM clones and images.

2016-06-?? Tobias Gläßer (Version 0.9.6)
    * Merged changes from forks/contributors. Thanks you to all who contributed!

	* Fixed copy VM feature. The original VM's UI became unusable after copying.

	* Added support for the meson build system as an alternative to cmake.

	* New feature: Helpful dialog when no boot device could be found.

	* Fixed ugly(low contrast) fonts in Info and VM tabs when using dark themes. (reported by gavsiu)

	* New feature: An overview of the new VM is now shown on the "Finish" page of the New VM Wizard.

	* Changed reset/save icons to fit better with Stop/Pause/Shutdown/... buttons.

	* New feature: Button for sending ACPI shutdown request called "Shutdown".
	  In contrast to the "Stop" button, this will allow users to cleanly shutdown VMs.

	* New feature enabled through new service capability: VMs now keep running when closing the main window.

	* Added service capability, which allows users to start/stop and generally manipulate VMs
	  from the command line and/-or over DBus.

